    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that \"bubble\" is so tiny and fragile. it's like we're just delaying the inevitable by a fraction of a second. if the end result is always going to be zero, then the energy we spend struggling through the pain and the mess of living just seems like a waste of resources. if everything is just a temporary anomaly, is there really any logical reason to keep fighting the descent? wouldn't it be more efficient to just... let go and accept the equilibrium?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
